Question
Hi all. I'm running into an issue with a Iceberg + MinIO S3 and I've exhausted all options trying to solve it. This is my last resort :/
I have Flink job that constantly writes to Iceberg. Everything works fine until the job reaches a runtime of 3 hours, then I get an S3 Invalid signature error.
After doing some research, it seems that org.apache.iceberg.aws.s3.S3FileIO generates a presigned URL for S3 auth which expires after 3 hours.
All I want is the ability to refresh this auth, or really have any working auth setup that allows me to run a Flink job for weeks at-a-time without running into this issue. Unfortunately, solving this problem has been more difficult than I would have anticipated.
Am I doing something wrong here? Or is there a simple solution to this S3 auth expiration issue?
I consulted with good ole chat gippity, which suggested I'd need to write my own credential provider or table loader that handles refresh, which is wild for such basic functionality. Flink is designed for long-running streaming jobs, so how do others get around this issue?
Here's a simple example of my code
Flink v1.17.2
Iceberg + iceberg-aws-bundle v1.6.1
// RabbitMQ Config
RMQConnectionConfig connectionConfig = new RMQConnectionConfig.Builder()
                .setHost("rabbitmq")
                .setPort(5672)
                .setUserName("guest")
                .setPassword("guest")
                .setVirtualHost("/")
                .build();

// RabbitMQ Flink Source
RMQSource<RowData> rmqSource = new RMQSource<>(
                connectionConfig,
                "MyQueue",
                false,
                new MyQueueDeserializer());

// Add RabbitMQ Source
DataStream<RowData> myStream = env
                .addSource(rmqSource)
                .setParallelism(1)
                .returns(TypeInformation.of(RowData.class));

// REST Catalog setup
Map<String, String> catalogProperties = new HashMap<>();
catalogProperties.put("type", "iceberg");
catalogProperties.put("catalog-type", "rest");
catalogProperties.put("uri", "http://nessie:19120/iceberg");
catalogProperties.put("ref", "main");
catalogProperties.put("property-version", "1");
catalogProperties.put("warehouse", "s3://warm-iceberg-data/warehouse");
catalogProperties.put("io-impl", "org.apache.iceberg.aws.s3.S3FileIO");
catalogProperties.put("s3.endpoint", "http://minio:9000");
catalogProperties.put("s3.region", "us-east-1");
catalogProperties.put("s3.path-style-access", "true");
catalogProperties.put("aws.access-key-id", "minioadmin");
catalogProperties.put("aws.secret-access-key", "minioadmin");

CatalogLoader catalogLoader = CatalogLoader.rest(
        "my_iceberg_catalog",
        hadoopConf, // Empty hadoop conf
        catalogProperties);

TableLoader tableLoader = TableLoader.fromCatalog(
        catalogLoader,
        TableIdentifier.of("my_db", "my_table"));

FlinkSink.forRowData(myStream)
        .tableLoader(tableLoader)
        .append()
        .name("Iceberg Sink");

Any assistance would be much appreciated!
